    this.myVariable = true;
    this.isRed = true;
  }
}
```
In the above example, the `isRed` property is used to determine whether the elements in the template should be styled with the `red` class or not. The `isRed` property is initially set to `false`, and the `red` class is not applied to the elements in the template.

When the `changeMyVariable()` method is called, the `isRed` property is set to `true`, and the `red` class is added to the elements in the template. This will change the styles of the elements to make them appear red.

Note that you can add CSS styles to the `red` class in a separate stylesheet or in the template itself to define the styles that should be applied when the class is present.

