```python
def bubble_sort(arr):
    n = len(arr)
    for i in range(n):
        unsorted = True
        for j in range(n-i-1):
            if arr[j] > arr[j+1]:
                arr[j], arr[j+1] = arr[j+1], arr[j]
                unsorted = True
            else:
                unsorted = False
                break
        if unsorted:
            continue
        return arr
```

This implementation uses a simple bubble sort algorithm, which compares adjacent elements in the array and swaps them if they are in the wrong order. It continues to loop until no more swapping is necessary. The time complexity of this algorithm is O(n^2) because it takes O(n) time to compare each pair of adjacent elements and there are O(n) pairs of elements to compare. This function can be made more efficient by using a different sorting algorithm, such as merge sort or quick sort, but those algorithms would have higher time complexities in the worst case.

