function p3(arr, k) {
  let counts = {};
  let sorted_arr = [];
  let distinct_arr = [];

  // Count occurrences of each element in arr
  for (let x of arr) {
    if (counts[x] === undefined) {
      counts[x] = 1;
    } else {
      counts[x] += 1;
    }
  }

  // Sort the histogram
  for (let x in counts) {
    sorted_arr.push([x, counts[x]]);
  }
  sorted_arr.sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1]);

  // Extract distinct elements
  for (let i = 0; i < k; i++) {
    distinct_arr.push(sorted_arr[i][0]);
  }

  return distinct_arr;
}
```

The function p3 takes two arguments, arr and k, where arr is the original array and k is the number of distinct elements to be returned. It first counts the occurrences of each element in arr using a histogram (counts). The histogram is sorted by the number of occurrences of each element (sorted_arr). Finally, it extracts the distinct elements from the sorted_arr and returns them in a new array (distinct_arr).

